body: "> All production and test implementation code is Rust and the distributed binaries have no Node.js, Bun, JavaScript, or TypeScript runtime dependency\n>\n> The CLI and SDK expose a versioned compatibility matrix against the latest published pm CLI and SDK contracts\n>\n> Shared language-neutral conformance fixtures prove byte-compatible TOON, JSON, history, merge, locking, transaction, and recovery behavior\n>\n> Linux, macOS, and Windows binaries pass unit, integration, property, fuzz, performance, fresh-project, migration, and installed-binary acceptance gates\n\n- `README.md` and `Cargo.toml` establish native binary and library entry points. The repository retains authored TypeScript test tooling, including `scripts/crash-harness.test.mts` and `tests/oracle/admission-oracle.mts`. Resolve the spec's test implementation requirement explicitly.\n- PR #181 and `tests/oracle/package.json` pin 2026.11.18. The published JS CLI/SDK package was at 2026.11.24 at audit time. Refresh the bounded parity matrix against the current published contracts and identify any remaining differences.\n- `docs/COMPATIBILITY.md` documents native record/output and recovery evidence. The real Git branch integration checks native-emitted records through the published merge driver. Add or identify language-neutral fixture receipts covering the full named byte-compatibility scope, with native merge and transaction boundaries explicit.\n- GitHub Actions run 45002344483 supplies historical Linux, macOS and Windows release and latency evidence. `justfile` and `.github/workflows/ci-deep.yml` cover part of the platform evidence. The full fuzz, migration and installed-binary acceptance matrix on all three platforms remains pending. Record the exact supported platform coverage and passing receipts for the missing gates. Existing #143 covers a separate macOS query-cost case.\n\nThe native feature tracker is `pm-rust-u4al`. The crate remains unpublished.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-24T19:12:43Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-rust#104 - Detect crash recovery divergence with replayable native and published checks [merged]\n> unbraind/pm-rust#165 - Match pm-cli 2026.11.11 refusals and atomic lifecycle admission natively [closed]\n> unbraind/pm-rust#181 - Refresh native parity to pm-cli 2026.11.18 [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
